# EPDesk invariants (full text in RULES.md)

A false Ready is the worst failure. A line is Ready only when all six pass:

1. Right product: exact code or reviewer confirmation. Never a description match alone.
2. Right EPD: range or average EPDs, superseded versions, unit differences and assumed conversions need a reviewer's check.
3. Verified: generic data is not an EPD.
4. Standard and version meet the client's clause. +A1 under +A2 is Missing; an unstated version is Needs review.
5. Valid on the delivery date. An estimated or missing date is never Ready.
6. Every requirement is confirmed. Defaults and assumptions block Ready.

How to work here:

- This repository is the static demo: one `index.html`, no build step. It holds no rules.
- Statuses, matching, requirements and coverage come from `lib/epdesk-rules-<version>.js`, built from the `@epdesk/rules` package. Change rules there, never here.
- One change per request. After a change, load the sample bid and list every line whose status changed, before → after.
- Stop and ask if a change touches the visual design or needs a new dependency.
- Show confidence as High, Medium or Low, never as a percentage.
- No customer data anywhere in the repository.
